import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'..')
from con_helpers import *
save(2,7,"One Second, Four Workers, and the One Who Watches","When the loop fires, note the four workers as they pass: manas caught it, buddhi calls it a threat, ahaṁkāra made it about me, chitta wants to file it. Then notice that you can see all that, and rest there for one breath.",[
mc("A","An aunt says to Sarah, “Oh, you’ve changed your hair.” Her attention snaps to the aunt and everything else goes quiet. Which worker is this?",
 ["Manas, the radar: it detected the signal, narrowed and flagged this matters, not yet knowing its meaning.","Buddhi, the decider: it resolved the ambiguous remark into a definite meaning, she is criticising me.","Ahaṁkāra, the I-maker: it claimed the remark and turned the volume up, so it became a personal wound.","Chitta, the memory-field: it stored the impression on the pile of every earlier moment of feeling judged."],0,
 "Swamiji takes the four words slowly. Manas detects; buddhi collapses the ambiguity into “she is criticising me,” along a channel that years of similar moments had already carved: not a free choice but a conditioned one; ahaṁkāra makes it “I’ve let myself go”; chitta stores it on the whole pile and deepens the groove.",
 "Manas detects and flags","Part 1"),
mc("A","At midnight the aunt is long gone, yet Sarah is still suffering. What does Swamiji say is happening?",
 ["The loop runs on its own: she re-presents, re-interprets and re-claims the memory from within.","The remark is still being said, so Sarah is still receiving fresh input from the aunt and reacting to that.","The memory has faded, so what she feels is only the weak echo of an event that has almost been forgotten.","The aunt is responsible, so the cure is for Sarah to speak to the aunt and ask her to take back the words."],0,
 "No new input is needed: manas re-presents, buddhi re-interprets, usually adding fresh negative detail, ahaṁkāra re-claims, chitta stores the strengthened version. Sarah agrees that the replay is worse than the moment was, and Swamiji says it almost always is, because the replay compounds.",
 "The loop runs on stored material","Part 2"),
mc("U","What does Swamiji mean by saṁsāra in this lesson?",
 ["The self-feeding wheel of conditioned existence: not a punishment, just what loops do when left unwatched.","A place of punishment for wrongdoing, from which a person can escape only by a long and hard penance.","The ordinary world of daily life, which has nothing to do with the loops of the inner instrument.","A stage of life for the young, which a person leaves behind on growing older and becoming wise."],0,
 "It turns automatically, unless awareness steps in. Swamiji says to hold that unless: everything turns on it.",
 "Saṁsāra is the self-feeding wheel","Part 2"),
mc("U","Back in Lesson 1.1, experience was X plus Y. After Module 2, what does Swamiji say Y is?",
 ["The whole inner instrument and all stored in it: chitta’s grooves, buddhi’s habits, ahaṁkāra’s claims, manas’s biases.","A single thought that a person can correct, once it has been found and seen to be mistaken.","The outside world, as it is given to a person by the people and the events around them.","The Self, which is the same in every person and so cannot account for differences between them."],0,
 "Kai says Y is not a thought he can just correct but the whole riverbed, which is why he could not think his way out. The four words were just X; the suffering was Sarah’s Y meeting them. Swamiji calls this the most hopeful sentence in the module: X you usually cannot control, but Y can be tended, cleared and re-landscaped.",
 "Y is the whole conditioned instrument","Part 2"),
judge("“Sarah’s aunt gave her the suffering: the four words were the whole cause, and Sarah’s own inner instrument played no part.”",F,
 "The four words were just X. The suffering was Sarah’s Y meeting them: two people hear the same words and live in two different worlds because their instruments differ. The hopeful side is that the wheel can be slowed.",
 "The words were X; the suffering was Y","Part 2"),
mc("A","Kai realises that if he can watch manas react, buddhi decide and ahaṁkāra grab, he cannot only be those things. What does Swamiji call what watches?",
 ["The witness, the sākṣī: awareness that sees but is never seen as an object, through every turn.","The inner critic, the voice that narrates: the worker that comments on each reaction as it arises.","The charioteer, buddhi: the decider that holds the reins and steers the whole system on the road.","The aunt’s view of Sarah: the outside opinion that gives a person the sense of who they are."],0,
 "Swamiji says this is the most important thing said in the module. Sarah feels it in her body: the part watching the midnight replay is not in the replay. In the chariot of earlier weeks, the rider, the one the journey is for, is this witness, the Self.",
 "The witness behind the loop","Part 3"),
mc("A","James says he half assumed they were mapping the enemy. What does Swamiji answer about the inner instrument?",
 ["Not an enemy or a second reality, but the Self seen through the mind, like one light through coloured glass.","It is an enemy to be removed, so that the Self can shine out without anything to cloud or colour it.","It is a second reality, quite separate from the Self, and the two must be kept apart by effort.","It is an illusion, so that once it is seen through, the person has no more use for it and drops it."],0,
 "When you see the instrument clearly, what shines through it is recognised as what was there all along: one undivided awareness appearing as the whole drama of a personal life. The waves were always the ocean.",
 "The instrument is the Self seen through the mind","Part 3"),
mc("A","Kai says he does not feel like a serene witness; he feels like the loop. How does Swamiji respond?",
 ["No pretence: the witness is already here, and recognising it begins by watching the loop uncaught.","He must manufacture the witness by effort, since it is a state that needs to be reached and kept up.","He must stop being a person, since the witness cannot be known by anyone while a personal self remains.","He must wait for a special experience, since the witness is revealed only at rare moments in a life."],0,
 "The witness is the very thing reading these words. Each time you watch the loop without being caught in it, even for a breath, you are resting briefly as the awareness the loop had been hiding. Not an escape from life, a different relationship to it. It was reached, Swamiji says, not by belief but by looking.",
 "The witness is already here","Part 3"),
judge("“The one-breath witness practice asks you to stop the loop when it fires and to force the tight chest to go away.”",F,
 "The practice is not to stop the loop. You silently note the four workers as they pass, manas caught it, buddhi is calling it a threat, ahaṁkāra has made it about me, chitta wants to file it, and notice that you can see all of that, so you are also the one watching. Rest there for one breath. For Kai: the awareness is not the one failing the seminar; it is just watching.",
 "Do not stop the loop: note it and rest as the watcher","Practical situation"),
mc("A","At the next family gathering a remark lands and Sarah’s chest tightens. What does Swamiji ask her to do?",
 ["Run it once: radar, decider, I-maker, memory, and I can see them all; one breath as the witness.","Win the moment, by answering the remark so well that the aunt has nothing more to say about it.","Leave the gathering, so as to be alone with the feeling and let it pass before she goes back in.","Say nothing and feel nothing, so that the remark has no effect and the loop never gets a chance to start."],0,
 "James is to do the same when a class triggers the old dread, teaching the next minute from the witness and not the wheel: stepping into the rider’s seat before picking up the reins.",
 "Name the four, then rest as the one who sees","Practical situation")])
